---
import Layout from "@/components/layout/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About">
	<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-4xl flex-col gap-6 p-8">
		<h1 class="text-primary font-display text-4xl font-extrabold">
			About Scouting411
		</h1>

		<p class="text-sm">
			Scouting411 is the unofficial front page of Scouting America. It gathers
			the news and resources that Scouting America publishes at the national
			level and puts them in one place, so that you can see everything at once
			instead of checking a dozen sites to find out what changed.
		</p>

		<p class="text-sm">
			Official Scouting information is scattered. It lives across program blogs,
			newsrooms, committee publications, and PDF libraries, each with its own
			site, its own update schedule, and its own idea of how to notify you.
			Plenty of it is genuinely useful and almost none of it is easy to find.
			This site exists to fix that. It does not replace any of those sources; it
			pulls everything together into a central hub and puts the data into one
			accessible format.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-2 font-serif text-xl font-bold">Where the data comes from</h2>

		<p class="text-sm">
			Everything here is published by Scouting America. Scouting411 does not
			write news or create resources of its own; it collects, organizes, and
			links back to the original, which is always the national, authoritative
			version.
		</p>

		<p class="text-sm">
			News is pulled automatically from official feeds and refreshed once a day,
			so an item may be up to 24 hours behind its source. You can see every feed
			being tracked on the{" "}
			<a
				href="/news/sources"
				class="text-primary wrap-anywhere hyphens-auto hover:underline"
			>
				sources
			</a>{" "}
			page, and how much has been collected from each on the{" "}
			<a
				href="/news/stats"
				class="text-primary wrap-anywhere hyphens-auto hover:underline"
			>
				stats
			</a>{" "}
			page. The{" "}
			<a
				href="/resources"
				class="text-primary wrap-anywhere hyphens-auto hover:underline"
			>
				resources
			</a>{" "}
			directory works differently. It is a hand-curated list of official tools,
			resources, and websites, chosen to surface the things you will find
			useful.
		</p>

		<p class="text-sm">
			Inclusion is limited to official Scouting America publications at the
			national level. Nothing from councils, districts, units, or third parties
			is listed, however good it may be, because the goal of this site is to
			give you official, canonical information. The full criteria are in the{" "}
			<a
				href="https://github.com/scouting-commons/scouting411#adding-a-resource"
				rel="noopener noreferrer"
				target="_blank"
				class="text-primary wrap-anywhere hyphens-auto hover:underline"
			>
				project README
			</a>
			. If something official is missing,{" "}
			<a
				href="https://github.com/scouting-commons/scouting411/issues/new/choose"
				rel="noopener noreferrer"
				target="_blank"
				class="text-primary wrap-anywhere hyphens-auto hover:underline"
			>
				suggest it
			</a>
			.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-2 font-serif text-xl font-bold">Who runs this</h2>

		<p class="text-sm">
			I'm a Scoutmaster. I built Scouting411 because I kept losing track of
			announcements that mattered to my unit, and because the answer to "where
			was that published?" was never the same place twice. It is a volunteer
			project, and it is free.
		</p>

		<p class="text-sm">
			Scouting411 is a project of{" "}
			<a
				href="https://scoutingcommons.org"
				rel="noopener noreferrer"
				target="_blank"
				class="text-primary wrap-anywhere hyphens-auto hover:underline"
			>
				Scouting Commons
			</a>
			, a home for free, community-built tools and open data for the Scouting
			community, built in the open by Scouts and Scouters.
		</p>

		<p class="text-sm">
			The site is open source under the AGPL-3.0 license. You can read the code,
			file an issue, or send a pull request on{" "}
			<a
				href="https://github.com/scouting-commons/scouting411"
				rel="noopener noreferrer"
				target="_blank"
				class="text-primary wrap-anywhere hyphens-auto hover:underline"
			>
				GitHub
			</a>
			.
		</p>

		<p class="text-sm">
			Scouting411 is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Scouting
			America. All trademarks and published content belong to their respective
			owners. This is an independent project, and any mistake you find here is
			mine rather than theirs. If you spot one, please report it.
		</p>
	</div>
</Layout>
